{"title":"MHT CET","category":"Engineering","bank":"mht_cet","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Sets and Relations","count":13,"questions":[{"id":64124,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Sets and Relations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"MHT CET","q":"Let $S$ be a non-empty subset of $\\mathbb{R}$. Consider the following statement:\np : There is a rational number $x \\in \\mathrm{~S}$ such that $x\\gt0$.\nWhich of the following statements is the negation of the statement p?","options":["There is a rational number $x \\in \\mathrm{~S}$ such that $x \\leq 0$.","There is no rational number $x \\in \\mathrm{~S}$ such that $x \\leq 0$.","Every rational number $x \\in \\mathrm{~S}$ satisfies $x \\leq 0$.","$x \\in \\mathrm{~S}$ and $x \\leq 0 \\Rightarrow x$ is not a rational number."],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Given statement is } \\\\\n& \\\\\n& \\exists x \\in \\mathrm{~S} \\text {, such that } x\\gt0 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\sim(\\exists x \\in \\mathrm{~S}, \\text { such that } x\\gt0) \\\\\n& \\equiv \\forall x \\in \\mathrm{~S}, x \\leq 0\n\\end{aligned}$\ni.e., Every rational number $x \\in S$ satisfies $x \\leq 0$.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"MHT CET 2024 (16 May Shift 1)","_marksId":"6792143b0aee93fa0796df03"},{"id":64125,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Sets and Relations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"MHT CET","q":"If $n(A)=4, n(B)=2$. Then the number of subsets of the set $\\mathrm{A} \\times \\mathrm{B}$ each having at least 3 elements are","options":["275","510","219","256"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{A})=4, \\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{B})=2 \\\\ & \\therefore \\quad \\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{A} \\times \\mathrm{B})=4 \\times 2=8 \\\\ & \\text { Required numbers }={ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_3+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_4+\\ldots+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_8 \\\\ &=2^8-\\left({ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_0+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_1+{ }^8 \\mathrm{C}_2\\right) \\\\ &=256-37 \\\\ &=219\\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"MHT CET 2024 (15 May Shift 1)","_marksId":"679214130aee93fa0796ddc9"},{"id":64126,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Sets and Relations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"MHT CET","q":"The given circuit is equivalent to\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fmht_cet%252FMbEYCI1htgKCfE1IXW4MFN8jHta0OXTjwjhIoRTeCpo.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmht_cet%2FMbEYCI1htgKCfE1IXW4MFN8jHta0OXTjwjhIoRTeCpo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmht_cet%2FMbEYCI1htgKCfE1IXW4MFN8jHta0OXTjwjhIoRTeCpo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fmht_cet%252F4wadTwDttKcCkDbL4yZpuDPrm5df0evBs5LiEdhOZEc.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmht_cet%2F4wadTwDttKcCkDbL4yZpuDPrm5df0evBs5LiEdhOZEc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fmht_cet%2F4wadTwDttKcCkDbL4yZpuDPrm5df0evBs5LiEdhOZEc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fmht_cet%252F3NdQr1OEjhzCg81hc5-EZiWGDaP8OpbUIxCAQodWBj4.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/